(4757384, 682726, 53572, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=657243" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657243.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657243.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657243.jpg"/></a> an intellectually fascinating shot, well composed and exposed.  i think i do wish the tones were a little richer.  what i do love is the perversity <i>(for those who confuse perverse with pervert: perversity = contrariness: deliberate and stubborn unruliness and resistance to guidance or discipline)</i> of covering the eyes in a portrait.  that, plus the implications of pure/impure are very interesting.  keeping pure from corrupting influences, or keeping the subject''s corruption from escaping.  nicely done.</td>', ' an intellectually fascinating shot, well composed and exposed.  i think i do wish the tones were a little richer.  what i do love is the perversity (for those who confuse perverse with pervert: perversity = contrariness: deliberate and stubborn unruliness and resistance to guidance or discipline) of covering the eyes in a portrait.  that, plus the implications of pure/impure are very interesting.  keeping pure from corrupting influences, or keeping the subject''s corruption from escaping.  nicely done.', '2008-06-08 06:00:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757385, 681647, 53572, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=657242" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657242.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657242.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657242.jpg"/></a> this image just grabbed me.  the strong flash light works in this context, adding a harshness and unblinking gaze to the picture.  the  face of the man, with the makeup and tears, goes against society''s traditional idea of a ''man'', yet is obviously male.  the composition works extremely well indeed, with the conjoining angles energising the whole piece.  a highly charged and emotional shot.</td>', ' this image just grabbed me.  the strong flash light works in this context, adding a harshness and unblinking gaze to the picture.  the  face of the man, with the makeup and tears, goes against society''s traditional idea of a ''man'', yet is obviously male.  the composition works extremely well indeed, with the conjoining angles energising the whole piece.  a highly charged and emotional shot.', '2008-06-08 06:01:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757386, 682684, 53572, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=657241" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657241.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657241.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/53572/120/657241.jpg"/></a> your new style of working is really resonating with me greatly.  the colours and tones in this one are simply gorgeous - rich and jewel-like.  the awareness and use of negative space are superb, with the emptiness and subject balancing each other in perfect unevenness.  the graininess works very well too, and the repetition of the man''s profile, positive and negative, left and right, is wonderful.</td>', ' your new style of working is really resonating with me greatly.  the colours and tones in this one are simply gorgeous - rich and jewel-like.  the awareness and use of negative space are superb, with the emptiness and subject balancing each other in perfect unevenness.  the graininess works very well too, and the repetition of the man''s profile, positive and negative, left and right, is wonderful.', '2008-06-08 06:02:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757480, 681647, 22459, '<td valign="top">This image scored a 4.6???? This can only reflect the lack of creativity and knowledge of the voters.........shame on you the 14 ones.</td>', 'This image scored a 4.6???? This can only reflect the lack of creativity and knowledge of the voters.........shame on you the 14 ones.', '2008-06-08 08:34:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4758977, 682915, 37858, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Louis.  I actually like this one even better than your earlier shot.  Great beard too.</td>', 'Congrats, Louis.  I actually like this one even better than your earlier shot.  Great beard too.', '2008-06-09 03:50:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4759206, 682539, 25355, '<td valign="top">Great character study - even if he is out of character. ;-Þ</td>', 'Great character study - even if he is out of character. ;-Þ', '2008-06-09 10:01:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4759255, 681883, 34462, '<td valign="top">What a handsome chap he is. Very nice portrait... I don''t understand the score but the portrait is good.</td>', 'What a handsome chap he is. Very nice portrait... I don''t understand the score but the portrait is good.', '2008-06-09 10:24:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760036, 682729, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I typically don''t care for straight on portraits, but his expression makes up for it.  That is funny.<br/> <br/>Technically, the bw works well (especially if his lips were orange, though that might have been interesting as well).  A touch brighter may have made it seem less "gray," and if the focus had been sharper, it would be a bit more compelling, I think.<br/> <br/>Overall, I feel you met the challenge well, and think your score is a bit lower than I would have expected.<br/> <br/>Best to you in future challenges.<br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I typically don''t care for straight on portraits, but his expression makes up for it.  That is funny. Technically, the bw works well (especially if his lips were orange, though that might have been interesting as well).  A touch brighter may have made it seem less "gray," and if the focus had been sharper, it would be a bit more compelling, I think. Overall, I feel you met the challenge well, and think your score is a bit lower than I would have expected. Best to you in future challenges.Karma', '2008-06-09 18:18:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761282, 682915, 28764, '<td valign="top">Very clean Black and White portrait. I like your camera too!</td>', 'Very clean Black and White portrait. I like your camera too!', '2008-06-10 10:51:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761906, 682004, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Very well done self portrait.  I like the "closeness" of it, and the fact that you haven''t felt it necessary to include all of the head.  That really forces attention to the eyes.  <br/> <br/>Also, I think that you have done a superb job with the focus, lighting, contrast, etc. in this shot.  It is technically very well done, and a strong image.  <br/> <br/>I think what might be missing is something for the viewer to connect with.  While I like the clean background, sometimes having something there helps to provide a context for the shot that this doesn''t have.  Also, your expression is largely indecipherable, but you look a bit nervous/unsure of yourself.  Not enough to for the viewers to relate to, but you don''t look completely relaxed, either.<br/> <br/>Again, I think this was a strong image that met the challenge well.  Best to you in future challenges.<br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Very well done self portrait.  I like the "closeness" of it, and the fact that you haven''t felt it necessary to include all of the head.  That really forces attention to the eyes.   Also, I think that you have done a superb job with the focus, lighting, contrast, etc. in this shot.  It is technically very well done, and a strong image.   I think what might be missing is something for the viewer to connect with.  While I like the clean background, sometimes having something there helps to provide a context for the shot that this doesn''t have.  Also, your expression is largely indecipherable, but you look a bit nervous/unsure of yourself.  Not enough to for the viewers to relate to, but you don''t look completely relaxed, either. Again, I think this was a strong image that met the challenge well.  Best to you in future challenges.Karma', '2008-06-10 18:05:23.000000', NULL, 0);
